cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference this verifier, formal proofs, or empirical interoperability
  datasets in IETF standards discussions or technical research, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
title: "SCITT Time-Anchor Triple-Engine Verifier"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ismail
    given-names: Shady
repository-code: "https://github.com/shady-ismail-titan/scitt-time-anchor-ietf127"
url: "https://shady-ismail-titan.github.io/scitt-time-anchor-ietf127/"
abstract: >-
  Clean-room, zero-dependency reference verifiers for
  draft-fassbender-scitt-time-anchor-08 and a hardened strict consensus and
  deterministic-encoding profile implemented across Python 3, safe Rust
  (#![forbid(unsafe_code)]), and zero-import offline WebAssembly, accompanied by
  Z3 SMT invariant proofs, a 64-variant CBOR framing-space empirical harness,
  and a multi-vendor interoperability suite.
keywords:
  - IETF
  - SCITT
  - OpenTimestamps
  - COSE
  - CBOR
  - Bitcoin
  - WebAssembly
  - RFC 9921
  - RFC 9942
  - RFC 9943
  - formal-verification
  - draft-fassbender-scitt-time-anchor
  - draft-templeman-scitt-framing-space
